res={
"unit":"theme-go-miscompile","profiles":[],
"findings":[{
 "ref":"new",
 "title":"Five go-ethereum family nodes run a Go toolchain with a published silent dead store miscompile, and no function on the opcode or state path has the triggering shape",
 "chainIds":GOAFF,"lens":"L1","assumptions":["A10"],"effect":"degrade","actor":"operator","severity":"info",
 "difference":"Go issue 81863: from Go 1.26.0 through go1.26.10 and from Go 1.27.0 through go1.27.3, the dead auto elimination pass attributes a CondSelect of two local addresses to its first operand only, so a store through a pointer that a branch chose between two non-escaping locals is deleted when the first local is never read, even if the other one is. It applies on every architecture whose compiler emits CondSelect (amd64, arm64, ppc64le, loong64, wasm). The fix is go1.26.11 and go1.27.4, released 2026-11-10. Today Arbitrum One answers as nitro v3.13.0-rc.9 linux-arm64 go1.27.3, Robinhood Chain as the same release on linux-arm64 and linux-amd64 with go1.27.3, Polygon (publicnode) as five bor v2.11.1-private builds with go1.26.10, BNB Smart Chain as Geth/v1.8.2 linux-amd64 go1.26.10, and Avalanche as avalanchego 1.15.3 go=1.26.10. Elysium reports go1.25.12 and the Celo op-geth backend go1.24.13, which predate the faulty pass order.",
 "mechanism":"The miscompile needs four things in one function after inlining: two stack allocated locals whose address is taken, a pointer that a side effect free if or if-else picks between their addresses, a store, zeroing or copy through that pointer and no load through it (branchelim refuses a CondSelect whose result feeds a load address), and a later direct read of the second local. A scan of holiman/uint256 v1.3.2 and v1.2.4 (all of uint256.go, mod.go, div.go, conversion.go, decimal.go) and of core/vm instructions.go, interpreter.go, stack.go, memory.go, evm.go, eips.go and core/state journal.go, transient_storage.go, statedb.go, state_object.go, access_list.go of the nitro fork 0e44603, bsc v1.8.2, bor v2.11.1 and libevm d398bc4dbe41 found no such function. The only branch selected pointers are: uint256 AddMod (x = &tmpX, y = &tmpY, v1.3.2 lines 240-245), where one operand is the caller's pointer, the pointers are only loaded from, and branchelim therefore keeps the Phi; SMod and SDiv, where the branch calls Neg and so is not side effect free and the pointer is only passed to Mod or Div; DivMod (m = new(Int).Set(m)) with a side effect in the branch; bor's interrupt flag in Run, loaded atomically and passed to runSwitch; the jump table choice in evm.go, which takes addresses of globals; and journal mutation state, which is heap memory. Sqrt in v1.2.4 swaps two pointers in a loop, which branchelim does not touch, and no opcode calls Sqrt. A dropped store in these functions would change the ADDMOD, SDIV or SMOD result, so those operands were run: 6,000 ADDMOD vectors with a modulus of at least 2^192 and each operand above, equal to or below the modulus, 6,112 SDIV and SMOD vectors over all sign pairs, plus the 99,985 battery and 85,544 targeted vectors. On each of the five networks every request was a JSON-RPC batch of web3_clientVersion and eth_call. There was no mismatch on any build. The PoolManager reaches SDIV and SMOD in TickBitmap.compress and Pool.tickSpacingToMaxLiquidityPerTick and MULMOD in FullMath and SqrtPriceMath; ADDMOD appears only in the compiler's metadata trailer.",
 "impact":"No path by which an ordinary account takes or freezes funds was found. If an unread function of the node held the shape, a node built with an affected toolchain would compute another state than one built with a fixed toolchain, which is a consensus fault of the operators and not something an attacker can aim at a pool through the PoolManager.",
 "preconditions":"Block producers would have to run an affected build and some function on the state transition path outside the files read would have to contain the shape. Neither is shown. The sequencer and validator builds are not published.",
 "mitigations":"Ask the Arbitrum, Robinhood Chain, Polygon, BNB Smart Chain and Avalanche operators to rebuild with go1.26.11 or go1.27.4 or later. Rerun paired.py after their next release.",
 "coreRefs":["src/libraries/TickBitmap.sol:20-27","src/libraries/Pool.sol:576-578","src/libraries/FullMath.sol:24","src/libraries/SqrtPriceMath.sol:252"],
 "sources":[
  {"url":U,"supports":"Issue 81863: the reproducer with p chosen between &x and &y and a store through p that is lost; bisected to CL 685676 of July 2025; called a silent wrong answer miscompile; backports to 1.26 and 1.27 requested."},
  {"url":FIX,"supports":"Fix commit 00ba484, 'teach deadstore about CondSelect': adds OpCondSelect to the keep rule in deadstore.go and the test fixedbugs/issue81863.go."},
  {"url":B1,"supports":"1.26 backport merged to release-branch.go1.26 as c7bed29 on 2026-10-27."},
  {"url":B2,"supports":"1.27 backport merged to release-branch.go1.27 as 8b28706 on 2026-10-27."},
  {"url":REL,"supports":"go1.26.10 and go1.27.3 released 2026-10-19 with crypto/x509 fixes only; go1.26.11 and go1.27.4 released 2026-11-10 with compiler fixes."},
  {"url":C.format(t='go1.27.3',f='deadstore.go'),"supports":"go1.27.3 deadstore.go line 333 keeps autos that reach Phi but not CondSelect; the go1.27.4 file has OpCondSelect, and go1.26.10 line 320 lacks it while go1.26.11 has it."},
  {"url":C.format(t='go1.25.12',f='compile.go'),"supports":"In go1.25.12 branchelim runs after dead auto elim (lines 477-480), so no CondSelect exists when that pass runs; in go1.26.10 and go1.27.3 branchelim runs before it (compile.go 479-481 and 480-482)."},
  {"url":C.format(t='go1.27.3',f='config.go'),"supports":"haveCondSelect is set for amd64, arm64, ppc64le, loong64 and wasm, so both builds the nodes report are affected."},
  {"url":C.format(t='go1.27.3',f='branchelim.go'),"supports":"branchelim does not make a CondSelect whose value feeds a load address and requires trivial if or if-else blocks."},
  {"url":UR,"supports":"uint256 v1.3.2 AddMod lines 215-266, udivrem 520-581, MulMod 720-750, SDiv 789-809, SMod 668-683, Lsh, Rsh, SRsh, ExtendSign 1042-1290: no store through a pointer selected between two locals."},
  {"url":UR2,"supports":"uint256 v1.2.4 AddMod 198-249, SMod 636-651, Sqrt 1306-1340: same result."},
  {"url":cv,"supports":"Builds that answered: Arbitrum One linux-arm64 go1.27.3 (397 chunks); Robinhood Chain linux-arm64 and linux-amd64 go1.27.3 (393 chunks by both, 4 by one); Polygon five bor v2.11.1-private go1.26.10 builds; BSC Geth/v1.8.2 go1.26.10; Avalanche avalanchego 1.15.3 go=1.26.10. 197,641 vectors per network, 0 mismatches, 0 errors."}],
 "evidence":"primary"}],
"cleared":[
 {"chainIds":[42161,4663],"lens":"L1","check":"Nitro fork 0e44603 core/vm opcode handlers and core/state journal and transient storage for the Go issue 81863 shape.","result":"Arithmetic handlers take pointers into the heap stack via pop1Peek1 (instructions.go 34-85), so no local address reaches uint256. journal.go 192-194, 262-264 and 313-315 select between a map entry and a new heap object. evm.go 164-195 picks the address of a global jump table. No store through a pointer chosen between two locals.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OffchainLabs/go-ethereum/0e44603/core/vm/instructions.go"},
 {"chainIds":[56,137],"lens":"L1","check":"bsc v1.8.2 and bor v2.11.1 core/vm and core/state for the shape.","result":"Handlers pass &x of a popped copy to uint256 (bsc instructions.go 29-181, bor 30-202) but each address is a single fixed local. bor Run (interpreter.go 123-126) picks between evm.interrupt and new(atomic.Bool) with a zeroing store in the branch and then loads it atomically and passes it to runSwitch, so the address counts as used. Push handlers (bor 1044-1072) write through one pointer on both branches.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/0xPolygon/bor/v2.11.1/core/vm/interpreter.go"},
 {"chainIds":[43114],"lens":"L1","check":"libevm d398bc4dbe41 core/vm and core/state and uint256 v1.2.4 for the shape.","result":"Same handlers as upstream with a z.IsZero guard in opAddmod (instructions.go 174-181) that writes through the stack pointer on both branches; NewEVMInterpreter picks addresses of global tables (interpreter.go 60-82). uint256 v1.2.4 AddMod and SMod behave as v1.3.2. No function has the shape.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ava-labs/libevm/d398bc4dbe41/core/vm/instructions.go"},
 {"chainIds":[99901,42220],"lens":"L1","check":"Is the Elysium nitro build (go1.25.12) or the Celo op-geth backend (go1.24.13) affected by Go issue 81863.","result":"No. The bug needs branchelim to run before dead auto elim, which began with CL 685676 on master in July 2025 (Go 1.26). In go1.25.12 compile.go branchelim runs after dead auto elim. Both versions were read from web3_clientVersion on 2026-11-24.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/go/+/refs/tags/go1.25.12/src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/compile.go?format=TEXT"},
 {"chainIds":[1,10,8453,130,7777777,480,57073,1868,196,143,4326,4217,5042,999],"lens":"L1","check":"Does any other network's endpoint report a Go toolchain.","result":"No. web3_clientVersion on 2026-11-24 reports reth, op-reth, base-reth, world-chain, xlayer reth, Monad, mega-reth, tempo, arc/v1 and hyperliquid evm, none of which is a Go program. Polygon's networks.json endpoint polygon.drpc.org reports Geth/v10.0.0/drpc, a proxy name, so publicnode was used for bor.","source":"research/network-risk/cycles/010/theme-go-miscompile.work/clientversions.json"},
 {"chainIds":GOAFF,"lens":"L1","check":"ADDMOD, SDIV and SMOD vectors aimed at the only branch selected pointers in uint256 (AddMod tmpX and tmpY, SMod and SDiv sign branches), on every build that answered.","result":"12,112 shape vectors plus 185,529 battery and targeted vectors per network, each request paired with web3_clientVersion: 0 mismatches on nitro linux-arm64 and linux-amd64 go1.27.3, five bor go1.26.10 builds, two BSC geth go1.26.10 builds and avalanchego go=1.26.10.","source":"research/network-risk/cycles/010/theme-go-miscompile.work/paired.json"}],
"leads":[
 {"chainIds":GOAFF,"lens":"L1","question":"With a go1.27.3 or go1.26.10 toolchain outside the repository, does go build -gcflags=-d=ssa/check_bce or an SSA dump of uint256, core/vm, core/state, trie, rlp and crypto/keccak show any CondSelect of two LocalAddr values feeding a Store, Zero or Move?","why":"This review could only read source; inlining can create the shape across function boundaries in packages that were not read (trie, rlp, keccak, arbos, Parlia, Bor consensus).","priority":"low"},
 {"chainIds":GOAFF,"lens":"L1","question":"Which Go version do the Arbitrum and Robinhood sequencers and the Polygon, BSC and Avalanche validators build with, and have they moved to go1.26.11 or go1.27.4?","why":"Only public RPC builds are known; a consensus difference would come from block producers.","priority":"low"}],
"leadResults":[
 {"leadId":"L-591","outcome":"cleared","answer":"Go issue 81863 is confirmed from the tracker and the fix diff: go1.27.0 to go1.27.3 are affected on amd64 and arm64, fixed in go1.27.4. No function in the nitro fork 0e44603 core/vm and core/state files read, nor in uint256 v1.3.2, has the shape (store through a pointer selected between two locals with no load through it). 197,641 vectors on Arbitrum One (arm64) and on both Robinhood builds matched. The sequencer toolchain is not published."},
 {"leadId":"L-611","outcome":"cleared","answer":"go1.26.0 to go1.26.10 are affected, fixed in go1.26.11. bor v2.11.1, bsc v1.8.2, libevm d398bc4dbe41, uint256 v1.3.2 and v1.2.4 have no function with the shape; the branch selected pointers that exist (AddMod, SMod, SDiv, DivMod, bor interrupt) are loaded from, passed to calls or chosen with side effects, which keeps them out of the miscompile. No toolchain was available to compile. Vectors aimed at those functions matched on every bor, BSC and avalanchego build that answered. Validator toolchains are not published."}]}
